          "label": "<p>Which layer of the epidermis is present ONLY in thick skin of the palms and sole</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which layer of the epidermis is present ONLY in thick skin of the palms and soles?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Stratum basale</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The stratum basale is the deepest epidermal layer, present in all skin types. It houses stem cells and melanocytes.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Stratum granulosum</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The stratum granulosum is present in both thick and thin skin. It contains keratohyalin granules that contribute to the waterproof barrier.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Stratum lucidum</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The stratum lucidum is a translucent layer found exclusively in thick skin, lying between the stratum granulosum and the stratum corneum.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Stratum corneum</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The stratum corneum is the outermost protective layer present in all skin types, though it is notably thicker in thick skin.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The answer is stratum lucidum. Thick skin on the palms and soles has five epidermal layers; thin skin elsewhere has only four — the lucidum is the one that is absent."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! The stratum lucidum is the extra fifth layer that distinguishes thick skin (palms and soles) from thin skin, which has only four epidermal layers."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
                "enableSolutionsButton": true,
